diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index 4746b0d..8899145 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -38,3 +38,18 @@ Return `200` with `text/plain` or `text/html` to send a reply, or `204` to
 send nothing. For longer-running commands, return `204` promptly, then POST
 UTF-8 text to `room.reply_to` when ready. Treat that URL as a credential.
 Redirects aren't followed, and private network targets are blocked.
+
+## Cooldowns and suspension
+
+Each bot can post 10 messages in a rolling 10-second window across all rooms,
+including webhook replies. The next post is rejected and starts a 30-second
+cooldown. API clients receive `429 Too Many Requests` and should wait at least
+the number of seconds in `Retry-After` before retrying. Webhook replies during
+cooldown are dropped. Five further posting attempts in the same cooldown
+suspend the bot.
+
+Ten consecutive failed webhook deliveries also suspend a bot. Any `2xx` response
+resets the streak, even when it produces no reply. Suspended bots receive no
+webhooks and cannot post (`403 Forbidden`), but keep their messages, memberships
+and place in the owner's bot allowance. An administrator can review the reason
+and select **Reactivate** on the Chat bots page to resume with fresh limits.
